  "summary": "In 653 the Tang dynasty issued the Yonghui Code with commentaries, after Emperor Gaozong decreed in 652 that commentaries be compiled. It is the oldest preserved complete law code in Chinese history, and Princeton University Press calls it the most important legal text in East Asian history.",
